1.created a project folder
2.installed python and django extensions
3.in terminal python --version
4.now we have to create a virtual environment for that 
        cmd:python -m venv venv
5.activate the environment
        cmd: .\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
6.now upgrade pip versions
        cmd: python -m pip install --upgrade pip
7.now install django 
        cmd: python -m pip install django
8.check its version
        cmd: python -m django --version
9.now start the django project 
        cmd: django-admin startproject config .
this cmd create basic structure needed for the django website
10.create intial database
        cmd: python manage.py migrate
